<title>USA: Alberto-Culver acquisition adds to earnings.</title>
<headline>Alberto-Culver acquisition adds to earnings.</headline>
<dateline>MELROSE PARK, Ill. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alberto-Culver Co said Thursday its acquisition of St. Ives Laboratories and its Swiss Formula brands, completed in February 1996, added more than $100 million to the fiscal year's sales and was accretive to earnings for the year.</p>
<p>The personal products company reported earnings for the September 30 fourth quarter rose to $0.67 per primary share from $0.56 a year ago. Sales gained to $431.1 million from $364.9 million.</p>
<p>Full-year earnings per diluted share rose to $2.11 from $1.87 and sales rose 17.1 percent to $1.59 billion.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
